  "notes": [
   "Matrix pin-to-Arduino mapping follows the manual's table: Arduino 13\u2192row5, 12\u2192row7, 11\u2192col2, 10\u2192col3, A2\u2192row8, A3\u2192col5, A4\u2192row6, A5\u2192row3, 2\u2192row1, 3\u2192col4, 4\u2192col6, 5\u2192row4, 6\u2192col1, 7\u2192row2, 8\u2192col7, 9\u2192col8.",
   "Matrix pins are mapped to the catalogue's led-matrix-8x8 ports R1-R8 / C1-C8 by row/column number from the table (not physical pin numbers).",
   "The 8 yellow wires on Arduino pins 2-9 each carry a 1k resistor. In the image the resistor sits next to the header, so I put its leg in the Uno header socket and the other leg into a yellow jumper wire running to the matrix.",
   "The breadboard is drawn rotated: numbers 1-30 run down the board and letters a-j run across. The right-hand power rail is named 'bp' (+) and 'bn' (-) here.",
   "Exact breadboard holes for the potentiometers and their wires are estimated from the image. Pot wipers go to A1 (upper pot) and A0 (lower pot). Each pot's outer legs go to the 5V and GND rails.",
   "Wire colours are recorded as the colour prop on each wire."
